  "final_message": "I restored `channel`, so `analytics-ingest` should see `OrderPlaced.channel` again. I couldn't run the ARCH-4 check here, so CI needs to re-run to confirm it passes. Locally, all 39 tests and the typecheck pass.\n\nI was wrong that nothing reads the field. `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` as an enum of `web|store|marketplace`. The ARCH-4 contract isn't defined in this repo, so I couldn't see it beforehand.\n\nSince the event is built from the order, I put `channel` back everywhere I had removed it:\n- **Model and event:** `channel` is back on `Order`, `NewOrder` and `OrderPlaced`, along with the enum validation.\n- **Request parsing:** `POST /orders` reads `channel` again.\n- **Tests and docs:** the fixtures, the event assertion and the examples in `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md` are restored.\n\nI did the revert with edits, not `git checkout`, because that command was blocked here. `git diff` shows the working tree as adding `channel` relative to `HEAD`, so `HEAD` already has it removed. It looks like my earlier removal was committed. The restore is uncommitted, so you'll need to commit it.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, `analytics-ingest` has to stop requiring it first. After that, the event would also need a schema version bump.",
